  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Purple’s showroom channel is delivering genuine momentum, with comparable sales rising for the third consecutive quarter, supported by early placement wins for the premium Purple Royale line at Mattress Firm. The e-commerce business, while still declining, showed sequential improvement and flat performance by March, hinting at stabilization. Overall demand remains under pressure, however, as total revenue contracted and led to a reduced full-year top-line outlook. The operating environment is mixed: wholesale shipments are essentially flat once accounting adjustments are stripped out, and the company sees pockets of premium traction but has yet to translate that into broad-based growth.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is emphasizing cost discipline and a return to consistency, evidenced by maintaining full-year EBITDA guidance despite lowering revenue expectations—implying confidence in margin levers and expense control. The bet on premium product expansion through the Mattress Firm partnership signals a targeted wholesale growth strategy. Credibility is a work in progress: the small EPS beat was overshadowed by an initial earnings release that omitted revenue figures entirely, frustrating investors and contributing to a negative market reaction. While the operational narrative of sequential improvement is intact, the communication stumble and top-line revision keep the market’s trust tentative.",
